From: BlackF1re <plevickij57@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:20:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 70/70] pinctrl: qcom: ssbi-mpp: honor GPIO output state

The SSBI MPP driver populates its software state from the bootloader.  When
an MPP is inherited as a bidirectional digital pin, selecting output mode
does not clear the input flag.  The update path consequently keeps encoding
the pin as bidirectional, and a requested output value is ignored.  The
GPIO direction callback also ignores its value argument.

This is observable on Sony Hikari, where PM8901 MPP1 is inherited in
bidirectional mode and controls the external 5 V source for USB host VBUS.
The regulator core reports the supply enabled while the physical enable pin
remains low.

Make both generic output configuration paths select output-only mode and
record the requested value before programming the MPP.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <plevickij57@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c
index 45d94932d..645a0f8fb 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c
@@ -390,4 +390,5 @@ static int pm8xxx_pin_config_set(struct pinctrl_dev *pctldev,
 		case PIN_CONFIG_LEVEL:
+			pin->input = false;
 			pin->output = true;
 			pin->output_value = !!arg;
 			break;
@@ -453,6 +454,7 @@ static int pm8xxx_mpp_direction_output(struct gpio_chip *chip,
 
 	switch (pin->mode) {
 	case PM8XXX_MPP_DIGITAL:
+		pin->input = false;
 		pin->output = true;
 		break;
 	case PM8XXX_MPP_ANALOG:
@@ -465,6 +467,8 @@ static int pm8xxx_mpp_direction_output(struct gpio_chip *chip,
 		break;
 	}
 
+	pin->output_value = !!value;
+
 	pm8xxx_mpp_update(pctrl, pin);
 
 	return 0;
